"aye"},{"name":"Wendy Askew","party":"Liberal","person_id":"tvfy_10914","person_slug":"wendy-askew","vote":"aye"}],"name":"Matters of Urgency - Regional Security - Former PM Paul Keating","noes":12,"question":"The majority voted in favour of a [motion](https://www.openaustralia.org.au/senate/?id=2023-03-20.129.1) moved by South Australian Senator [Simon Birmingham](https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/people/senate/sa/simon_birmingham) (Liberal), which means it passed. These motions don't make any legal changed on their own, but they are politically influential as they represent the will of the Senate. ### Motion text > *That, in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a matter of urgency:* > > *The need for the Senate to recognise that AUKUS expresses Australia's ambition for enduring peace and prosperity in our region, and to reject criticism from former Prime Minister Paul Keating that it is the worst deal in our history.*","result":"affirmative","slug":"division-federal-senate-7999","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2023-03-20/5"}
